the nobel prize for medicine goes to  three biochemists who live and work in  the united states  the nobel assembly at kerlinski  institute has today decided to award the  2013 nobel prize in physiology or  medicine  jointly  to james rothman randy schechtman and  thomas hudov  how do cells in the body transport  molecules like insulin what jeans and  markers ensure that these substances  arrive at the right place at the right  time  decades of research enabled the three  scientists to answer those fundamental  questions german-born thomas sudhof is a  professor at stanford university he  hails from gutingen and has been working  in the united states for 30 years  james rothman researches at yale  and randy shekman is at the university  of california at berkeley the call from  sweden woke him in the middle of the  night  hello i didn't even have a chance to  look at the clock to see when it was  and uh picked up the phone and this very  distinctive swedish accent of goron  hansen who's the chairman of the  medicine prize committee called  and he  congratulated me he assured me that this  was not a hoax  implications the three winners will  receive their prize at a ceremony in  stockholm on december 10th and they'll  share the purse of almost 1 million  euros
 

